<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  th, td {
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: left;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
  th {
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
    font-weight: bold;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin: 0;">FAU</h1>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0;">COLLEGE FOR</h2>
        <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0;">DESIGN AND</h2>
        <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0;">SOCIAL INQUIRY</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 14px; margin: 0;">SCHOOL OF CRIMINOLOGY & CRIMINAL JUSTICE</h3>
      <p style="margin: 2px 0;">{{ employer.address_line_1 }}</p>
      <p style="margin: 2px 0;">{{ employer.address_line_2 }}</p>
      <p style="margin: 2px 0;">tel: {{ employer.phone }}</p>
      <p style="margin: 2px 0;">fax: {{ employer.fax }}</p>
      <p style="margin: 2px 0;">web: {{ employer.website }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 30px;">MEMORANDUM</h2>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>To: <span data-field="recipient.name">{{ recipient.name }}</span></p>
    <p>From: <span data-field="sender.name">{{ sender.name }}</span></p>
    <p>Subject: <span data-field="subject">{{ subject }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>Date: <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span></p>
    <p>RE: <span data-field="re_subject">{{ re_subject }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>The School of Criminology and Criminal Justice is very excited to submit a revised curriculum for our Bachelor of Arts in Criminal Justice. The revised curriculum proposal is a result of much collaboration, feedback, planning, and months of discussion among our faculty; and our CCJ faculty approved it unanimously at our October 14, 2011 meeting.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 style="font-size: 16px;">The revised curriculum will:</h3>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
      <li>Improve the structure and academic rigor of our bachelor's degree to better prepare our students for the complexities of today's workforce, and also to equip them for graduate studies should they choose to pursue an advanced degree.</li>
      <li>Reduce redundancy across our course offerings by eliminating courses whose subject matter is covered in other classes, or that have been determined to be extraneous to the goals of our School's vision.</li>
      <li>Remove variability in the quality of learning that a student experiences over the course of their tenure at FAU. Our goal is to ensure that students receive education in the most important discipline-specific concepts rather than simply a cursory overview of a hodgepodge of criminal justice topics.</li>
      <li>Constrain the paths our students can take in terms of course offerings. This is not intended to lessen student choices of career possibilities, but rather to help them make informed decisions based on their career interests. Previously, our</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p>students took three core courses and then filled their remaining upper-level major requirements with 21 elective credits. In our revised program – which will be available to students in the Fall of 2012 – students will take four core courses (12 credit hours), and then two of five restricted electives (6 credit hours), followed by four of sixteen free electives (for the final 12 credit hours).</p>
    <p>The revised curriculum does not require additional faculty resources, or new course proposals. Please find attached our revised curriculum proposals for your decision.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 12px; text-align: center;">
    <p>Boca Raton • <span data-field="department_contact_1">{{ department_contact_1 }}</span> • <span data-field="department_contact_2">{{ department_contact_2 }}</span> • <span data-field="department_contact_3">{{ department_contact_3 }}</span> • <span data-field="department_contact_4">{{ department_contact_4 }}</span></p>
    <p>An Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Bachelor of Arts in Criminal Justice</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 50%;">Prerequisite</th>
        <th style="width: 50%;">Current Curriculum</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>CCJ 2002 - Required for freshmen OR what the School deems equivalent to the previously-existing CCJ 2002 (The Criminal Justice System) at the community college level.</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Core Courses: 12 Credit Hours</td>
        <td>Core Courses: 9 Credit Hours</td>
      </tr>
      {% for course in core_courses %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ course.code }} - {{ course.name }}</td>
        <td>{{ course.current_code }} - {{ course.current_name }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr>
        <td>Restricted Electives: 6 Credit Hours</td>
        <td>Free Electives: 21 credit hours</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Students are required to take two of the following five restricted elective courses:</td>
        <td>Students should take seven of the following twenty-four elective courses:</td>
      </tr>
      {% for elective in restricted_electives %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ elective.code }} - {{ elective.name }}</td>
        <td>{{ elective.current_code }} - {{ elective.current_name }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
      <tr>
        <td>Free Electives: 12 credit hours</td>
        <td>Free Electives: 12 credit hours</td>
      </tr>
      {% for free_elective in free_electives %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ free_elective.code }} - {{ free_elective.name }}</td>
        <td>{{ free_elective.current_code }} - {{ free_elective.current_name }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>